Assertions:
[REL] PERCENT_1 is greater than PERCENT_0 after order 1 alone -- the counter is not all-or-nothing {DOC}
[DOM] no 'Completed' chip is present on the card after order 1 alone -- target is 2, one order has not reached it {SPEC}
[REL] PERCENT_2 is greater than PERCENT_1 after order 2, and PERCENT_2 = 100 within the 30s settle budget {DOC}
[DOM] a 'Completed' chip is present on the card after order 2 {SPEC}
[DOM] an Earned row for amount = @td(MSN_E2E_ORDERCOUNT.reward) is present in the transactions list, dated after ORDER_2_NUMBER's confirmation -- this attributable row is the proof the grant happened, not the raw balance figure {SPEC}
[MATH] BAL_AFTER - BAL_BEFORE >= @td(MSN_E2E_ORDERCOUNT.reward) -- a lower bound that still fails if the reward was never granted, but does not assume no other Earned activity occurred on the same account in the same window {DOC}
[STATE] ORDER_1_NUMBER and ORDER_2_NUMBER are present and distinct -- the journey placed two real, separate orders {OBSERVED}

[MATH] PERCENT_CART_ONLY = PERCENT_0 -- adding the target quantities to cart alone does not move progress {DOC}
[REL] PERCENT_AFTER is strictly greater than PERCENT_CART_ONLY -- completing the purchase is what moves it {DOC}
[MATH] PERCENT_AFTER = 100 given the order alone satisfied both target quantities in full {SPEC}
[DOM] the reopened modal's aggregate summary reads 'Targets met 2 / 2' (or the store's equivalent all-targets-met copy) and names the unlocked reward points -- this is the ONLY completion surface the modal has; there is no per-row 'target met' indicator to check {OBSERVED}
[STATE] the cart held the added quantities before checkout (CART_QTY_A_0/CART_QTY_B_0 reflect the pre-add state, confirming the earlier cart-only add was real and still did not move progress) {OBSERVED}

[REL] TOTAL is greater than SUBTOTAL -- the order genuinely carries the platform's tax leg, so subtotal and total are distinguishable observations on this run's own order {OBSERVED}
[MATH] SUBTOTAL = @td(MSN_E2E_ORDERVALUE_003.measured_subtotal) and TOTAL = @td(MSN_E2E_ORDERVALUE_003.measured_total) -- this run's order reproduces the exact figures the fixture was derived from {OBSERVED}
[NEG] SUBTOTAL is below @td(MSN_E2E_ORDERVALUE_003.goal_target); TOTAL is at or above it -- the two readings genuinely disagree about whether this order qualifies {OBSERVED}
[MATH] PERCENT_AFTER = 100 -- the goal completed, which is only possible under the TOTAL reading {DOC}
[DOM] a 'Completed' chip is present on the card {SPEC}

[DOM] an Earned row for amount = @td(MSN_E2E_ORDERVALUE.reward) is present, dated after order 1's confirmation -- the attributable record the grant happened {SPEC}
[MATH] BAL_1 - BAL_0 >= @td(MSN_E2E_ORDERVALUE.reward) -- a lower bound: other store-wide missions may ALSO have granted on this fresh account's first order, so an exact-equality check would be a false failure, but the reward amount must be present regardless {DOC}
[MATH] BAL_2 = BAL_1 + EARN_2 - RDM_2 -- the final balance reconciles to the previous balance plus exactly the ledger entries order 2 produced. Order 2 is itself a Mixed Cart order, so BL-LOY-007(a) has it post its own Earned row and sibling missions may co-grant on it; an exact BAL_1 - PTS_LINE_TOTAL equality is therefore wrong here, while a balance that moves by anything OTHER than its own ledger rows -- a silent double debit, or a retry that deducted twice but logged once (BL-LOY-007d) -- still breaks this {BL}
[MATH] RDM_2 = PTS_LINE_TOTAL -- the reward is spent at exactly the PTS price of the line it paid for. This is the check the co-grant noise cannot absorb: EARN_2 sums Earned-type rows only, so a deduction of the wrong amount moves RDM_2 and nothing compensates for it {BL}
[COUNT] RDM_2_COUNT = 1 -- exactly one Redeemed entry for order 2 (BL-LOY-007b/d). A double deduction and a no-op deduction are each a different count, and neither is visible to an amount check on a single row {BL}
[STATE] both orders reached confirmation with distinct order numbers {OBSERVED}

[REL] ORDER_DISCOUNT is greater than 0 -- the coupon genuinely reduced the order {OBSERVED}
[MATH] ORDER_TOTAL = @td(MSN_E2E_ORDERVALUE_005.measured_total) -- this run's discounted order reproduces the exact figure the fixture was derived from {OBSERVED}
[NEG] ORDER_TOTAL is below @td(MSN_E2E_ORDERVALUE_005.goal_target), which sits below @td(MSN_E2E_ORDERVALUE_005.measured_total_undiscounted) -- the constructed boundary case genuinely straddles the target {OBSERVED}
[NEG] PERCENT_AFTER does NOT reach 100, and no 'Completed' chip is present, despite the pre-discount subtotal alone having exceeded the target {DOC}

[DOM] no error state, broken layout, or JS exception overlay is present on the missions page at DOM_1 or any later poll, whatever percent the card shows {OBSERVED}
[NEG] the card does NOT show a 'Completed' chip at any DOM_i where its own percent is below 100 {OBSERVED}
[REL] the sequence DOM_1..DOM_n is monotonically non-decreasing across the polls {OBSERVED}
[REL] at every paired read, DOM_i = API_i within rounding -- the storefront card is never observed to lag a same-moment direct read of the same mission {HYPOTHESIS}
[INV] the final poll within the 30s budget reads DOM = 100 with a 'Completed' chip present; if it does not, report BLOCKED -- settlement did not converge within budget, not a silent pass {OBSERVED}

[REL] PERCENT_AFTER is greater than PERCENT_0 -- the points-currency line moved the quantity target {DOC}
[MATH] PERCENT_AFTER = 100 -- the single target's whole quantity was satisfied by the PTS-priced line alone {DOC}
[DOM] a 'Completed' chip is present on the card {SPEC}

[MATH] BAL_1 - BAL_0 = @td(MSN_E2E_ORDERVALUE_008.reward_expected_total) -- the exact, seeder-measured co-grant total for this account's first order, not a lower bound {OBSERVED}
[MATH] BAL_2 = BAL_1 -- the balance is unchanged by the cancellation; the mission reward is not clawed back {HYPOTHESIS}
[NEG] the loyaltyPointsHistory entry count is unchanged after the cancellation -- a mission grant carries a null object with NO order reference at all (measured: all four mission rewards sit in the 17 null-object entries, while all 46 product-earn rows carry type CustomerOrder + orderNumber), so a row-referencing-ORDER_NUMBER check would pass vacuously; only a count delta can detect a reversal row {HYPOTHESIS}
[DOM] the mission card for @td(MSN_E2E_ORDERVALUE_008.name) still shows its 'Completed' chip after the order is cancelled {HYPOTHESIS}
